# CI-regenerated artifacts: during a rebase (pull.rebase is on, and VS Code's
# Sync pulls BEFORE pushing, so the .husky/pre-push hook never sees that
# flow), conflicts in these paths are always deterministic generator output —
# the local side ran over newer sources than the bot's, so the `regenlocal`
# merge driver takes the local version of the file outright and the pull
# completes without stopping. Anything the deploy regen finds off afterwards
# is normalized by its own push-back (deploy-docs.yml, "Commit regenerated
# content"). Paths outside this list keep ordinary merge behavior, so genuine
# conflicts still stop the rebase. Keep the list in sync with the workflows'
# push-back path lists and .husky/pre-push; packages/*/package.json (release
# version commits) is deliberately NOT listed.
#
# The driver itself lives in local git config — set automatically on every
# `pnpm install` by scripts/prepare.ts (linked worktrees share it):
#   git config merge.regenlocal.driver 'cp -- %B %A'
# During a rebase %B is the commit being replayed (the LOCAL work) — this
# direction assumes rebase pulls; a true `git merge` would flip it.
docs/src/** merge=regenlocal
packages/*/size.json merge=regenlocal
packages/*/README.md merge=regenlocal
/README.md merge=regenlocal
benchmark/results/** merge=regenlocal
packages/*/tests/visual/screenshots/** merge=regenlocal
packages/*/registry/** merge=regenlocal
